# Milestone: M3
# Covers: stack-exhausted exception is catchable; caught exception matches
#         Exception.Scheduling type via isA(); message includes location.
# defer-to: M4 (requires Exception.Scheduling type hierarchy and isA() method dispatch)
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture catches a stack-overflow via 'catch(var s if s.isA(Exception.Scheduling))'.
#   This requires: (1) a named exception type hierarchy (Exception.Scheduling) —
#   M4 stdlib object model; (2) isA() method dispatch on the exception value —
#   M4 prototype-OOP.  At M3 try/catch works but only with unguarded catch clauses
#   (no 'if cond' guard with method calls).  Stack-exhaustion detection is present
#   in the C runtime but the typed exception hierarchy is M4.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with exception type hierarchy):
# # function f() { f() } |;
# # try { f() } catch(var s if s.isA(Exception.Scheduling)) { echo(s) };
